      "page": 9,
      "what": "Collector at grid 3: the force at B from the A side is called tension, from the C side compression. One point has one sense. TD1 is pulled toward -x by the tension strut, so its +x chord (grid 3) is in compression; Ex 3.2 (p1, strut pushing) gives tension there.",
