  "assumptions": [
    {
      "what": "Load by band: at each depth the 200 plf is shared by the sheathed bands in proportion to their length. A-B: band 1-2 gets 200(25/125) = 40 plf, band 2-4 gets 200(100/125) = 160 plf. B-C: band 2-4 only, 200 plf. Each band is a simple beam across the depth between its own edges (1-2 spans A-B, 2-4 spans A-C).",
      "why": "Book method p4-p5; the tool must reproduce the band split to match the basic shears."
    },
